    "reasoning": "All 16 intended answers are supported by their own captured worked solutions. q-143078: inverse-square dependence and increasing intensity give dI/dt=k/d² with k>0. q-80147: the amplitude is sqrt(8+16)=2sqrt(6), and the phase is arctan(sqrt(2))≈0.955; the source's final equality should be an approximation because the phase is rounded. q-8723: the roots are -arctan(2) and π-arctan(2), whose product rounds to -2.252. q-65229: factoring sin(theta) leaves sin²(theta)+cos²(theta)=1; the omitted theta in one intermediate source expression is a typographical error. q-119392: the numerator becomes cos(x)sin(x)+1, giving cot(x)+csc²(x), on the original domain sin(x)≠0. q-87840 and q-87834: the even powers are nonnegative, so both inequalities hold for every real x. q-7905: B reverses A's shear, while E=A and A² has entry -10 below the diagonal; only I and III hold. q-102666: A has determinant 3 and inverse B; C=3B, so AC=CA=3I and only I holds. q-7627: the captured solution specifies center (3,-1) and radii 2 and 4, which give option 3; the supplied image has no readable coordinate labels, so those coordinates cannot be independently checked from the image alone. q-170189: dx/dy=1-9/y⁴=-8 at y=1, giving slope -1/8 and tangent y=-x/8+3/2. q-115031: cubing the isolated cube root preserves order and gives x≤13. q-87508: combining 3x+1≥0 with 3x+1≤9 gives [-1/3,8/3]. q-87781: combining 4x+3≥0 with 4x+3≤16 gives [-3/4,13/4]. q-115205: e^(x-2)<1 gives x<2. q-87833: division by ln(0.84)<0 reverses the inequality, giving x<ln(20)/ln(0.84)-5. No submitted grades were supplied; MA evidence here consists of captured worked solutions.",
